---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PixelEdge from '../components/pixel/PixelEdge.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../site.config';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="What data this site collects, what it stores in your browser, and how to contact the owner.">
  <section class="sec sec-first sec-pad-b tone-a grid-bg" data-title="man page">
    <div class="wrap relative z-10">
      <p class="meta flex justify-between gap-4" aria-hidden="true"><span>PRIVACY(7)</span><span class="hidden sm:inline">{siteConfig.name} Manual</span><span>PRIVACY(7)</span></p>
      <h1 class="t-1 mt-14" data-reveal>privacy policy</h1>
      <dl class="mt-12 max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-[13px]" data-reveal>
        <div><dt class="px-font mb-2 text-[10px] text-accent">NAME</dt><dd class="pl-6">privacy — what data this site collects, what it keeps in your browser, and how to reach the owner</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="px-font mb-2 text-[10px] text-accent">AUTHOR</dt><dd class="pl-6">{siteConfig.author.name} &lt;{siteConfig.author.email}&gt;</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <PixelEdge to="b" seed={61} />
  </section>
  <section class="sec tone-b grid-bg" data-title="read" style="padding-top:clamp(4rem,9vh,7rem)">
    <div class="wrap"><div class="prose">
      <p>Short version: no cookies, no third-party scripts, no accounts. What little is saved stays in your browser.</p>
      <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
      <p>This site saves your theme choice, your effects preference and your roadmap quiz progress in your browser's local storage. This data never leaves your device unless you export it yourself. Clearing your browser storage removes all of it.</p>
      <h2>What is not collected</h2>
      <p>No cookies are set, no accounts exist, and nothing you type into the site is sent anywhere. Page requests do reach the hosting provider (Cloudflare Pages), which processes standard request logs as described in <a rel="noopener" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/trust-hub/">Cloudflare's trust hub</a>.</p>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>Cloudflare Web Analytics may be enabled, which is cookie-free and does not build individual profiles; it reports aggregate page views and referrers only. When enabled, no cookie banner is needed because there is nothing to consent to.</p>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>If advertising is ever enabled it would require cookies, and this page (plus a consent banner) will be updated before that happens. Until then: none.</p>
      <h2>Mail you send</h2>
      <p>Mail sent to the contact address is used to reply and, for corrections, to improve the article. It is never added to a list or shared.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.author.email}`}>{siteConfig.author.email}</a>.</p>
    </div></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
